#notebooks/CodeBlue_Prediction.ipynb‹™{
  "metadata": {
    "kernelspec": {
      "display_name": "Jupyter Notebook",
      "name": "jupyter"
    }
  },
  "nbformat": 4,
  "nbformat_minor": 5,
  "cells": [
    {
      "id": "752f4089-0ea0-41c1-9519-672f45c4402f",
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "metadata": {
        "codeCollapsed": true,
        "collapsed": false
      },
      "source": "# Code Blue Prediction Model & Critical Care Optimization Platform\n\nEnd-to-end Snowflake ML pipeline that predicts the likelihood of a Code Blue (cardiopulmonary arrest) event for hospitalized patients from demographics, flowsheet vitals and laboratory values. It supports early intervention, patient safety, ICU capacity planning and proactive clinical decision-making. Everything runs on warehouse compute (DEMO_WH) in DEMO_DB.CLINIC, with the Feature Store in DEMO_DB.FEATURES.\n\n**Table of contents**\n1. Training dataset creation (PATIENT_CODEBLUE, 1,000 synthetic encounters, last 3 months)\n2. Feature engineering (Snowpark) + Feature Store (FV_CODE_BLUE_PREDICTION v V1) + point-in-time training set\n3. AutoML-style training & evaluation - XGBoost, LightGBM, RandomForest, LogisticRegression, GradientBoosting - tracked in CODE_BLUE_EXPERIMENT\n4. Model Registry deployment - CODEBLUE_MODEL version V1_0 with metrics, params, feature definitions, explainability\n5. Production inference - CODEBLUE_SCORING_RESULTS\n6. Final business dataset - CODEBLUE_PREDICTION_RESULTS\n\n_Assumptions: version names must be SQL identifiers, so suggested v1.0 is registered as V1_0; the default model version is treated as the latest approved version._"
    },
    {
      "id": "3fba9e54-405c-4e1f-9918-6292c7570b84",
      "cell_type": "code",
      "metadata": {
        "language": "python",
        "title": "Setup: imports, session, constants"
      },
      "source": "import json, warnings\nimport numpy as np, pandas as pd\nfrom snowflake.snowpark.context import get_active_session\nfrom snowflake.snowpark import functions as F\nwarnings.filterwarnings('ignore')\n\nsession = get_active_session()\nDB, SCHEMA, WH = 'DEMO_DB', 'CLINIC', 'DEMO_WH'\nFEATURES = 'FEATURES'                      # Feature Store schema\nEXPERIMENT = 'CODE_BLUE_EXPERIMENT'\nMODEL_NAME, MODEL_VERSION = 'CODEBLUE_MODEL', 'V1_0'\nFQ_MODEL = f'{DB}.{SCHEMA}.{MODEL_NAME}'\nMON = f'{DB}.{SCHEMA}.CODEBLUE_MODEL_MONITOR'   # reserved name for a future model monitor\nFV_NAME, FV_VERSION = 'FV_CODE_BLUE_PREDICTION', 'V1'\nSEED = 42\nfor s in [f'USE WAREHOUSE {WH}', f'USE DATABASE {DB}', f'USE SCHEMA {SCHEMA}']:\n    session.sql(s).collect()\nprint(session.get_current_database(), session.get_current_schema(), session.get_current_warehouse())",
      "outputs": [],
      "execution_count": null
    },
    {
      "id": "fb27df75-751e-45b6-be85-f3e7d6b57d64",
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "metadata": {
        "codeCollapsed": false
      },
      "source": "## Phase 1 - Training dataset creation\nGenerates 1,000 synthetic encounters (admissions over the last 90 days). A latent acuity score drives correlated vitals and labs (high acuity: higher RR/pulse/BNP/BUN/neutrophils, lower SBP/SpO2/albumin/calcium). CODEBLUE is drawn from a clinically motivated logistic model (~6-9% prevalence). DISCHARGE_DATE is always populated and lengthens with acuity and Code Blue (recent admissions may have a projected discharge). About 3% of labs/vitals are set missing to exercise imputation. Patient, Flowsheet and Lab tables are joined on PRIMARYMRN."
    },
    {
      "id": "fba585f7-e36b-43bc-9933-6ac1e97d9375",
      "cell_type": "code",
      "metadata": {
        "language": "python",
        "title": "Phase 1: generate synthetic source tables and PATIENT_CODEBLUE"
      },
      "source": "rng = np.random.default_rng(SEED)\nN = 1000\nnow = pd.Timestamp.now().floor('h')\nmrn = [f'MRN{1000000 + i}' for i in range(N)]\nage = np.clip(rng.normal(62, 17, N), 18, 98).round().astype(int)\ngender = rng.choice(['Male', 'Female'], N, p=[0.49, 0.51])\nheight = np.where(gender == 'Male', rng.normal(176, 7, N), rng.normal(162, 6.5, N)).round(1)\nweight = np.clip(np.where(gender == 'Male', rng.normal(195, 40, N), rng.normal(165, 38, N)), 90, 450).round(1)\nbirth = [(now - pd.Timedelta(days=int(a * 365.25 + rng.integers(0, 365)))).normalize() for a in age]\nentry = now - pd.to_timedelta(rng.integers(0, 90 * 24, N), unit='h')\n\nacuity = rng.normal(0, 1, N) + 0.03 * (age - 62)\nresp = np.clip(rng.normal(17, 3, N) + 2.5 * acuity, 8, 40).round()\nsbp = np.clip(rng.normal(125, 16, N) - 9 * acuity, 60, 210).round()\ndbp = np.clip(sbp * 0.62 + rng.normal(0, 7, N), 35, 130).round()\ntemp = np.clip(rng.normal(37.0, 0.5, N) + 0.3 * acuity, 34.5, 41).round(1)\nspo2 = np.clip(rng.normal(96.5, 2, N) - 1.8 * acuity, 70, 100).round()\no2 = np.clip(np.where(spo2 < 93, rng.normal(4, 2, N), rng.exponential(0.6, N)), 0, 15).round(1)\npulse = np.clip(rng.normal(82, 13, N) + 9 * acuity, 40, 180).round()\nlymph = np.clip(rng.lognormal(0.3, 0.4, N) - 0.25 * acuity, 0.1, 6).round(2)\nneut = np.clip(rng.lognormal(1.5, 0.4, N) + 1.2 * acuity, 0.5, 30).round(2)\nalb = np.clip(rng.normal(3.8, 0.5, N) - 0.3 * acuity, 1.5, 5.2).round(1)\nbcult = (rng.random(N) < 1 / (1 + np.exp(-(-2.6 + 0.9 * acuity)))).astype(int)\nbnp = np.clip(rng.lognormal(4.6 + 0.6 * acuity, 0.9, N), 5, 5000).round()\nbun = np.clip(rng.lognormal(2.8 + 0.25 * acuity, 0.4, N), 4, 150).round()\nca = np.clip(rng.normal(9.2, 0.5, N) - 0.2 * acuity, 6.5, 11.5).round(1)\n\nlogit = (-4.3 + 1.2 * acuity + 0.05 * (resp - 17) - 0.02 * (sbp - 125) - 0.12 * (spo2 - 96.5)\n         + 0.015 * (pulse - 82) + 0.7 * bcult + 0.35 * np.log(bnp / 100) - 0.5 * (alb - 3.8))\ncodeblue = (rng.random(N) < 1 / (1 + np.exp(-logit))).astype(int)\nlos_days = np.clip(rng.gamma(2.0, 1.5 + 1.2 * np.maximum(acuity, 0), N) + 5 * codeblue + 0.5, 0.5, 45)\ndisch = entry + pd.to_timedelta((los_days * 24).round(), unit='h')\n\ndef with_missing(a, frac=0.03):\n    a = a.astype(float).copy(); a[rng.random(N) < frac] = np.nan; return a\n\npatient = pd.DataFrame({'PRIMARYMRN': mrn, 'BIRTHDATE': birth, 'GENDER': gender, 'AGE': age,\n    'HEIGHT_CMS': with_missing(height), 'WEIGHT_LBS': with_missing(weight),\n    'ENTRY_DATE': entry, 'DISCHARGE_DATE': disch, 'CODEBLUE': codeblue})\nflowsheet = pd.DataFrame({'PRIMARYMRN': mrn, 'RESPIRATION': with_missing(resp), 'SYSTOLIC_BP': with_missing(sbp),\n    'DIASTOLIC_BP': with_missing(dbp), 'TEMPERATURE': with_missing(temp), 'PULSE_OXIMETRY': with_missing(spo2),\n    'O2_FLOW_RATE': with_missing(o2), 'PULSE': with_missing(pulse)})\nlab = pd.DataFrame({'PRIMARYMRN': mrn, 'ABS_LYMPHOCYTE': with_missing(lymph), 'ABS_NEUTROPHIL': with_missing(neut),\n    'ALBUMIN': with_missing(alb), 'BLOOD_CULTURE': bcult, 'BNP': with_missing(bnp), 'BUN': with_missing(bun),\n    'CALCIUM': with_missing(ca)})\n\nfor name, d in [('SRC_PATIENT', patient), ('SRC_FLOWSHEET', flowsheet), ('SRC_VITAL_LAB', lab)]:\n    session.write_pandas(d, name, auto_create_table=True, overwrite=True, use_logical_type=True)\n\nsession.sql('''CREATE OR REPLACE TABLE PATIENT_CODEBLUE AS\nSELECT p.PRIMARYMRN, p.BIRTHDATE::DATE AS BIRTHDATE, p.GENDER, p.AGE, p.HEIGHT_CMS, p.WEIGHT_LBS,\n       p.ENTRY_DATE::TIMESTAMP_NTZ AS ENTRY_DATE, p.DISCHARGE_DATE::TIMESTAMP_NTZ AS DISCHARGE_DATE,\n       f.RESPIRATION, f.SYSTOLIC_BP, f.DIASTOLIC_BP, f.TEMPERATURE, f.PULSE_OXIMETRY, f.O2_FLOW_RATE, f.PULSE,\n       l.ABS_LYMPHOCYTE, l.ABS_NEUTROPHIL, l.ALBUMIN, l.BLOOD_CULTURE, l.BNP, l.BUN, l.CALCIUM,\n       p.CODEBLUE\nFROM SRC_PATIENT p JOIN SRC_FLOWSHEET f USING (PRIMARYMRN) JOIN SRC_VITAL_LAB l USING (PRIMARYMRN)''').collect()\nsrc = session.table('PATIENT_CODEBLUE')\nprint('rows:', src.count())\nsrc.group_by('CODEBLUE').count().show()",
      "outputs": [],
      "execution_count": null
    },
    {
      "id": "dc8c45e0-e816-4071-82e4-85e66f56cfc0",
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "metadata": {
        "codeCollapsed": true,
        "collapsed": false
      },
      "source": "### Phase 1 Deliverables\n| Deliverable | Where |\n|---|---|\n| PATIENT_CODEBLUE table | `DEMO_DB.CLINIC.PATIENT_CODEBLUE` (created above) |\n| Data profiling summary | `profile_summary` (cell below) |\n| Dataset statistics & schema documentation | `patient_schema` (SQL) + `schema_doc` (column dictionary) |"
    },
    {
      "id": "9f30e0e1-026f-4a57-93b1-382fe5fcd9bc",
      "cell_type": "code",
      "metadata": {
        "language": "python",
        "title": "Phase 1 deliverable: data profiling summary"
      },
      "source": "raw_pdf = src.to_pandas()\nnum_profile_cols = raw_pdf.select_dtypes('number').columns\nprofile_summary = pd.DataFrame({\n    'dtype': raw_pdf.dtypes.astype(str),\n    'non_null': raw_pdf.notna().sum(),\n    'null_pct': (raw_pdf.isna().mean() * 100).round(2),\n    'distinct': raw_pdf.nunique(),\n}).join(raw_pdf[num_profile_cols].describe().T[['mean', 'std', 'min', '50%', 'max']].rename(columns={'50%': 'median'}).round(2))\nprint(f'rows: {len(raw_pdf)} | columns: {raw_pdf.shape[1]} | CODEBLUE rate: {raw_pdf.CODEBLUE.mean():.1%} '\n      f'({int(raw_pdf.CODEBLUE.sum())} positives) | entry window: {raw_pdf.ENTRY_DATE.min()} -> {raw_pdf.ENTRY_DATE.max()}')\nprofile_summary",
      "outputs": [],
      "execution_count": null
    },
    {
      "id": "79ab7181-4d3d-4f8c-8647-3db9396e5290",
      "cell_type": "code",
      "metadata": {
        "language": "sql",
        "resultVariableName": "patient_schema",
        "title": "Phase 1 deliverable: PATIENT_CODEBLUE schema"
      },
      "source": "%%sql -r patient_schema\nSELECT ORDINAL_POSITION, COLUMN_NAME, DATA_TYPE, IS_NULLABLE, NUMERIC_PRECISION, NUMERIC_SCALE\nFROM DEMO_DB.INFORMATION_SCHEMA.COLUMNS\nWHERE TABLE_SCHEMA = 'CLINIC' AND TABLE_NAME = 'PATIENT_CODEBLUE'\nORDER BY ORDINAL_POSITION;",
      "outputs": [],
      "execution_count": null
    },
    {
      "id": "8518a9f5-c5eb-4c8c-a887-046435603f16",
      "cell_type": "code",
      "metadata": {
        "language": "python",
        "title": "Phase 1 deliverable: column dictionary"
      },
      "source": "col_desc = {\n    'PRIMARYMRN': ('Identifier', 'Patient medical record number (entity key)', '-'),\n    'BIRTHDATE': ('Demographic', 'Date of birth', 'date'), 'GENDER': ('Demographic', 'Male / Female', '-'),\n    'AGE': ('Demographic', 'Age at admission', 'years'), 'HEIGHT_CMS': ('Demographic', 'Height', 'cm'),\n    'WEIGHT_LBS': ('Demographic', 'Weight', 'lb'), 'ENTRY_DATE': ('Encounter', 'Admission timestamp', 'timestamp'),\n    'DISCHARGE_DATE': ('Encounter', 'Discharge timestamp', 'timestamp'),\n    'RESPIRATION': ('Vital', 'Respiratory rate', 'breaths/min'), 'SYSTOLIC_BP': ('Vital', 'Systolic blood pressure', 'mmHg'),\n    'DIASTOLIC_BP': ('Vital', 'Diastolic blood pressure', 'mmHg'), 'TEMPERATURE': ('Vital', 'Body temperature', 'deg C'),\n    'PULSE_OXIMETRY': ('Vital', 'Oxygen saturation SpO2', '%'), 'O2_FLOW_RATE': ('Vital', 'Supplemental oxygen flow', 'L/min'),\n    'PULSE': ('Vital', 'Heart rate', 'bpm'), 'ABS_LYMPHOCYTE': ('Lab', 'Absolute lymphocyte count', '10^3/uL'),\n    'ABS_NEUTROPHIL': ('Lab', 'Absolute neutrophil count', '10^3/uL'), 'ALBUMIN': ('Lab', 'Serum albumin', 'g/dL'),\n    'BLOOD_CULTURE': ('Lab', 'Blood culture positive (1) / negative (0)', 'flag'), 'BNP': ('Lab', 'B-type natriuretic peptide', 'pg/mL'),\n    'BUN': ('Lab', 'Blood urea nitrogen', 'mg/dL'), 'CALCIUM': ('Lab', 'Serum calcium', 'mg/dL'),\n    'CODEBLUE': ('Target', 'Code Blue event during encounter (1 = yes)', 'flag'),\n}\nschema_doc = pd.DataFrame([(c, *v) for c, v in col_desc.items()], columns=['COLUMN', 'CATEGORY', 'DESCRIPTION', 'UNIT'])\nschema_doc = schema_doc.merge(profile_summary[['dtype', 'null_pct', 'min', 'median', 'max']], left_on='COLUMN', right_index=True, how='left')\nschema_doc",
      "outputs": [],
      "execution_count": null
    },
    {
      "id": "a9968ce9-cd8b-4ae7-9121-d0484fcef600",
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "metadata": {
        "codeCollapsed": false
      },
      "source": "## Phase 2 - Feature engineering & Feature Store\nSnowpark pipeline (pushed down as SQL, so training and inference share identical logic via the feature view): median imputation (medians computed once and baked into the view), GENDER encoded with sklearn LabelEncoder mapping, derived clinical features (BMI, MAP, shock index, neutrophil-lymphocyte ratio, hypoxia flag), date features (LOS days, admission duration hours, day of week, month). Scaling: tree models are scale-invariant; StandardScaler is applied inside the LogisticRegression pipeline so it ships with the model. Note: LOS/discharge-based features are included per requirements but are only known at discharge (potential leakage for real-time use).\n\nFeature view FV_CODE_BLUE_PREDICTION version V1 (physical object FV_CODE_BLUE_PREDICTION$V1 = FV_CODE_BLUE_PREDICTION_V1) on entity PATIENT (PRIMARYMRN), timestamp ENCOUNTER_TS. Training set is built with point-in-time ASOF join via generate_training_set."
    },
    {
      "id": "40bf064c-313e-47ec-a944-1a7f2e31a431",
      "cell_type": "code",
      "metadata": {
        "language": "python",
        "title": "Phase 2: Snowpark feature pipeline + Feature Store + training set"
      },
      "source": "from sklearn.preprocessing import LabelEncoder\nfrom snowflake.ml.feature_store import FeatureStore, FeatureView, Entity, CreationMode\n\nsrc = session.table(f'{DB}.{SCHEMA}.PATIENT_CODEBLUE')   # fully qualified: Feature Store views live in another schema\nle = LabelEncoder().fit(src.select('GENDER').distinct().to_pandas()['GENDER'].dropna())\ngender_map = {g: int(i) for i, g in enumerate(le.classes_)}\nvitals = ['RESPIRATION', 'SYSTOLIC_BP', 'DIASTOLIC_BP', 'TEMPERATURE', 'PULSE_OXIMETRY', 'O2_FLOW_RATE', 'PULSE']\nlabs = ['ABS_LYMPHOCYTE', 'ABS_NEUTROPHIL', 'ALBUMIN', 'BLOOD_CULTURE', 'BNP', 'BUN', 'CALCIUM']\nnum_cols = ['AGE', 'HEIGHT_CMS', 'WEIGHT_LBS'] + vitals + labs\nmedians = src.select([F.median(c).alias(c) for c in num_cols]).to_pandas().iloc[0].to_dict()\n\ngexpr = F.lit(-1)\nfor k, v in gender_map.items():\n    gexpr = F.when(F.col('GENDER') == k, F.lit(v)).otherwise(gexpr)\nd = src\nfor c in num_cols:\n    d = d.with_column(c, F.coalesce(F.col(c).cast('double'), F.lit(float(medians[c]))))\nfeat_df = d.select(\n    'PRIMARYMRN', F.col('ENTRY_DATE').alias('ENCOUNTER_TS'),\n    *[F.col(c) for c in num_cols], gexpr.alias('GENDER_ENC'),\n    (F.col('WEIGHT_LBS') * 0.453592 / F.pow(F.col('HEIGHT_CMS') / 100, 2)).alias('BMI'),\n    ((F.col('SYSTOLIC_BP') + 2 * F.col('DIASTOLIC_BP')) / 3).alias('MEAN_ARTERIAL_PRESSURE'),\n    (F.col('PULSE') / F.col('SYSTOLIC_BP')).alias('SHOCK_INDEX'),\n    (F.col('ABS_NEUTROPHIL') / F.col('ABS_LYMPHOCYTE')).alias('NEUTROPHIL_LYMPH_RATIO'),\n    F.iff(F.col('PULSE_OXIMETRY') < 92, 1, 0).alias('HYPOXIA_FLAG'),\n    (F.datediff('hour', F.col('ENTRY_DATE'), F.col('DISCHARGE_DATE')) / 24.0).alias('LOS_DAYS'),\n    F.datediff('hour', F.col('ENTRY_DATE'), F.col('DISCHARGE_DATE')).alias('ADMISSION_DURATION_HRS'),\n    F.dayofweek('ENTRY_DATE').alias('ENTRY_DOW'), F.month('ENTRY_DATE').alias('ENTRY_MONTH'))\nfeat_df = feat_df.select('PRIMARYMRN', 'ENCOUNTER_TS', *[F.col(c).cast('double').alias(c) for c in feat_df.columns if c not in ('PRIMARYMRN', 'ENCOUNTER_TS')])\n\nfs = FeatureStore(session=session, database=DB, name=FEATURES, default_warehouse=WH, creation_mode=CreationMode.CREATE_IF_NOT_EXIST)\npatient_entity = Entity(name='PATIENT', join_keys=['PRIMARYMRN'], desc='Hospitalized patient encounter (PRIMARYMRN)')\ntry:\n    fs.register_entity(patient_entity)\nexcept Exception as e:\n    print('entity exists:', str(e)[:80])\nfv = FeatureView(name=FV_NAME, entities=[patient_entity], feature_df=feat_df, timestamp_col='ENCOUNTER_TS',\n                 desc='Code Blue predictors - demographics, vitals, labs, derived clinical and date features')\ngender_desc = 'LabelEncoder ' + ', '.join(f'{k}={v}' for k, v in gender_map.items())\nfv = fv.attach_feature_desc({'BMI': 'Body mass index kg per m2', 'SHOCK_INDEX': 'Pulse divided by systolic BP',\n    'MEAN_ARTERIAL_PRESSURE': 'SBP plus 2 x DBP over 3', 'NEUTROPHIL_LYMPH_RATIO': 'ANC divided by ALC',\n    'LOS_DAYS': 'Length of stay in days', 'GENDER_ENC': gender_desc})\nfv = fs.register_feature_view(feature_view=fv, version=FV_VERSION, overwrite=True)\n\nspine = src.select('PRIMARYMRN', F.col('ENTRY_DATE').alias('ENCOUNTER_TS'), 'CODEBLUE')\ntry:\n    train_sdf = fs.generate_training_set(spine_df=spine, features=[fv], spine_timestamp_col='ENCOUNTER_TS', spine_label_cols=['CODEBLUE'])\nexcept TypeError:\n    train_sdf = fs.generate_training_set(spine, [fv], 'ENCOUNTER_TS', ['CODEBLUE'])\ntrain_pdf = train_sdf.to_pandas()\nFEATURE_COLS = [c for c in train_pdf.columns if c not in ('PRIMARYMRN', 'ENCOUNTER_TS', 'CODEBLUE')]\nprint('training set:', train_pdf.shape, '| positives:', int(train_pdf.CODEBLUE.sum()))\nprint('features:', FEATURE_COLS)",
      "outputs": [],
      "execution_count": null
    },
    {
      "id": "c04c220e-37db-41dd-ac8d-c92b74c407c4",
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "metadata": {
        "codeCollapsed": true,
        "collapsed": false
      },
      "source": "### Phase 2 Deliverables\n| Deliverable | Where |\n|---|---|\n| Reusable Snowpark Python pipeline | `build_codeblue_features()` (cell below), validated against the registered feature view logic |\n| Feature transformation documentation | `feature_transform_doc` |\n| Feature list used for training | `training_feature_list` (from `FEATURE_COLS`) |"
    },
    {
      "id": "296567b2-2cdc-4df3-9436-aac325d4358b",
      "cell_type": "code",
      "metadata": {
        "language": "python",
        "title": "Phase 2 deliverable: reusable Snowpark feature pipeline"
      },
      "source": "def build_codeblue_features(df, medians: dict, gender_map: dict, num_cols: list = num_cols):\n    \"\"\"Snowpark (SQL pushdown) feature pipeline for Code Blue scoring.\n    df: Snowpark DataFrame with the PATIENT_CODEBLUE schema. medians/gender_map: training-time artifacts.\"\"\"\n    g = F.lit(-1)\n    for k, v in gender_map.items():\n        g = F.when(F.col('GENDER') == k, F.lit(v)).otherwise(g)\n    for c in num_cols:\n        df = df.with_column(c, F.coalesce(F.col(c).cast('double'), F.lit(float(medians[c]))))\n    out = df.select(\n        'PRIMARYMRN', F.col('ENTRY_DATE').alias('ENCOUNTER_TS'), *[F.col(c) for c in num_cols], g.alias('GENDER_ENC'),\n        (F.col('WEIGHT_LBS') * 0.453592 / F.pow(F.col('HEIGHT_CMS') / 100, 2)).alias('BMI'),\n        ((F.col('SYSTOLIC_BP') + 2 * F.col('DIASTOLIC_BP')) / 3).alias('MEAN_ARTERIAL_PRESSURE'),\n        (F.col('PULSE') / F.col('SYSTOLIC_BP')).alias('SHOCK_INDEX'),\n        (F.col('ABS_NEUTROPHIL') / F.col('ABS_LYMPHOCYTE')).alias('NEUTROPHIL_LYMPH_RATIO'),\n        F.iff(F.col('PULSE_OXIMETRY') < 92, 1, 0).alias('HYPOXIA_FLAG'),\n        (F.datediff('hour', F.col('ENTRY_DATE'), F.col('DISCHARGE_DATE')) / 24.0).alias('LOS_DAYS'),\n        F.datediff('hour', F.col('ENTRY_DATE'), F.col('DISCHARGE_DATE')).alias('ADMISSION_DURATION_HRS'),\n        F.dayofweek('ENTRY_DATE').alias('ENTRY_DOW'), F.month('ENTRY_DATE').alias('ENTRY_MONTH'))\n    return out.select('PRIMARYMRN', 'ENCOUNTER_TS',\n                      *[F.col(c).cast('double').alias(c) for c in out.columns if c not in ('PRIMARYMRN', 'ENCOUNTER_TS')])\n\nfeat_check = build_codeblue_features(src, medians, gender_map)\nassert feat_check.columns == feat_df.columns, 'column mismatch vs feature view logic'\nmismatched = feat_check.subtract(feat_df).count()\nprint(f'pipeline rows: {feat_check.count()} | columns: {len(feat_check.columns)} | rows differing from feature view logic: {mismatched}')",
      "outputs": [],
      "execution_count": null
    },
    {
      "id": "0fbf03c8-a07a-4d48-accb-8880c027b4d8",
      "cell_type": "code",
      "metadata": {
        "language": "python",
        "title": "Phase 2 deliverable: transformation docs and training feature list"
      },
      "source": "transforms = {\n    'GENDER_ENC': ('GENDER', 'LabelEncoder mapping ' + str(gender_map) + ', unknown = -1'),\n    'BMI': ('WEIGHT_LBS, HEIGHT_CMS', 'weight_lbs x 0.453592 / (height_cm/100)^2'),\n    'MEAN_ARTERIAL_PRESSURE': ('SYSTOLIC_BP, DIASTOLIC_BP', '(SBP + 2 x DBP) / 3'),\n    'SHOCK_INDEX': ('PULSE, SYSTOLIC_BP', 'PULSE / SBP'),\n    'NEUTROPHIL_LYMPH_RATIO': ('ABS_NEUTROPHIL, ABS_LYMPHOCYTE', 'ANC / ALC'),\n    'HYPOXIA_FLAG': ('PULSE_OXIMETRY', '1 if SpO2 < 92 else 0'),\n    'LOS_DAYS': ('ENTRY_DATE, DISCHARGE_DATE', 'hours between / 24 (known only at discharge - leakage risk)'),\n    'ADMISSION_DURATION_HRS': ('ENTRY_DATE, DISCHARGE_DATE', 'hours between (known only at discharge - leakage risk)'),\n    'ENTRY_DOW': ('ENTRY_DATE', 'day of week'), 'ENTRY_MONTH': ('ENTRY_DATE', 'month'),\n}\nrows = [(c, c, f'median imputation (fill = {medians[c]:.2f}), cast double', 'Raw') for c in num_cols]\nrows += [(f, s, t, 'Derived') for f, (s, t) in transforms.items()]\nfeature_transform_doc = pd.DataFrame(rows, columns=['FEATURE', 'SOURCE_COLUMNS', 'TRANSFORMATION', 'TYPE'])\n\ntraining_feature_list = pd.DataFrame({'FEATURE': FEATURE_COLS, 'DTYPE': [str(train_pdf[c].dtype) for c in FEATURE_COLS]})\ntraining_feature_list = training_feature_list.merge(feature_transform_doc[['FEATURE', 'TYPE']], on='FEATURE', how='left')\nprint(f'{len(FEATURE_COLS)} training features | feature view: {DB}.{FEATURES}.{FV_NAME}${FV_VERSION}')\ndisplay(feature_transform_doc)\ntraining_feature_list",
      "outputs": [],
      "execution_count": null
    },
    {
      "id": "98855845-082d-405d-937b-564297caeec2",
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "metadata": {
        "codeCollapsed": true,
        "collapsed": false
      },
      "source": "## Phase 3 - AutoML-style training & evaluation\nLeakage-free, cross-validated model selection:\n- **Leakage removed:** `LOS_DAYS` and `ADMISSION_DURATION_HRS` (known only at discharge, and synthetic LOS encodes the label) are excluded from `FEATURE_COLS`. They remain in the feature view but are not model inputs.\n- **80/20 stratified split** (seed 42). The 200-row test set is held out and used **only once** for final reporting.\n- **Per-family RandomizedSearchCV** (20 candidates x stratified 5-fold CV, ROC-AUC) on the training set for XGBoost (incl. `min_child_weight`, `colsample_bytree`, `reg_lambda`, `reg_alpha`, `gamma`), LightGBM, RandomForest, LogisticRegression (StandardScaler pipeline) and sklearn GradientBoostingClassifier.\n- **Class imbalance:** `scale_pos_weight` / `class_weight=balanced` / balanced sample weights.\n- **Champion = highest mean CV ROC-AUC**; CV std shows whether families are statistically tied. PR-AUC (average precision) reported alongside ROC-AUC.\n- Each family's best candidate is logged (params, CV and test metrics) to experiment `CODE_BLUE_EXPERIMENT`."
    },
    {
      "id": "c055035c-b92d-4c59-9361-d163e2d3acdd",
      "cell_type": "code",
      "metadata": {
        "language": "python",
        "title": "Phase 3: train, tune, evaluate, track experiment"
      },
      "source": "from sklearn.model_selection import train_test_split, StratifiedKFold, RandomizedSearchCV\nfrom sklearn.metrics import (accuracy_score, precision_score, recall_score, f1_score, roc_auc_score,\n                             average_precision_score, confusion_matrix)\nfrom sklearn.ensemble import RandomForestClassifier, GradientBoostingClassifier\nfrom sklearn.linear_model import LogisticRegression\nfrom sklearn.pipeline import Pipeline\nfrom sklearn.preprocessing import StandardScaler\nfrom sklearn.utils.class_weight import compute_sample_weight\nfrom xgboost import XGBClassifier\nfrom lightgbm import LGBMClassifier\nfrom snowflake.ml.experiment import ExperimentTracking\n\n# Drop features only known at discharge (they leak the label in this synthetic data)\nLEAKAGE_COLS = ['LOS_DAYS', 'ADMISSION_DURATION_HRS']\nFEATURE_COLS = [c for c in FEATURE_COLS if c not in LEAKAGE_COLS]\n\nX = train_pdf[FEATURE_COLS].astype('float64'); y = train_pdf['CODEBLUE'].astype(int)\nX_tr, X_te, y_tr, y_te = train_test_split(X, y, test_size=0.2, stratify=y, random_state=SEED)\nspw = float((y_tr == 0).sum() / max((y_tr == 1).sum(), 1))\ncv = StratifiedKFold(n_splits=5, shuffle=True, random_state=SEED)\nN_ITER = 20\n\nsearch_space = {\n 'XGBOOST': (XGBClassifier(scale_pos_weight=spw, random_state=SEED, eval_metric='logloss', n_jobs=1), {\n    'n_estimators': [100, 200, 300, 500], 'learning_rate': [0.01, 0.03, 0.05, 0.1], 'max_depth': [2, 3, 4, 5],\n    'subsample': [0.6, 0.7, 0.8, 1.0], 'colsample_bytree': [0.6, 0.7, 0.8, 0.9], 'min_child_weight': [1, 5, 10],\n    'reg_lambda': [1, 3, 5, 10], 'reg_alpha': [0, 0.1, 0.5, 1], 'gamma': [0, 0.1, 0.5, 1]}),\n 'LIGHTGBM': (LGBMClassifier(class_weight='balanced', subsample_freq=1, random_state=SEED, verbose=-1, n_jobs=1), {\n    'n_estimators': [100, 200, 300, 500], 'learning_rate': [0.01, 0.03, 0.05, 0.1], 'max_depth': [2, 3, 4, 5, -1],\n    'num_leaves': [7, 15, 31], 'min_child_samples': [5, 10, 20, 40], 'subsample': [0.6, 0.7, 0.8, 1.0],\n    'colsample_bytree': [0.6, 0.7, 0.8, 0.9], 'reg_lambda': [0, 1, 5, 10]}),\n 'RANDOMFOREST': (RandomForestClassifier(class_weight='balanced_subsample', random_state=SEED, n_jobs=1), {\n    'n_estimators': [200, 300, 500], 'max_depth': [4, 6, 8, 12, None], 'min_samples_split': [2, 5, 10, 20],\n    'min_samples_leaf': [1, 2, 5, 10], 'max_features': ['sqrt', 'log2', 0.5]}),\n 'LOGISTICREG': (Pipeline([('scaler', StandardScaler()), ('clf', LogisticRegression(class_weight='balanced', max_iter=5000))]), {\n    'clf__C': [0.001, 0.003, 0.01, 0.03, 0.1, 0.3, 1.0, 3.0, 10.0]}),\n 'GRADIENTBOOSTING': (GradientBoostingClassifier(random_state=SEED), {\n    'n_estimators': [100, 150, 200, 300], 'learning_rate': [0.01, 0.03, 0.05, 0.1], 'max_depth': [2, 3, 4],\n    'subsample': [0.6, 0.7, 0.8, 1.0], 'min_samples_split': [5, 10, 20, 40]}),\n}\n\nexp = ExperimentTracking(session=session, database_name=DB, schema_name=SCHEMA)\nexp.set_experiment(EXPERIMENT)\nstamp = pd.Timestamp.now().strftime('%m%d_%H%M%S')\nresults, models, cv_tables = [], {}, {}\nfor fam, (base, dist) in search_space.items():\n    n_cand = int(np.prod([len(v) for v in dist.values()]))\n    rs = RandomizedSearchCV(base, dist, n_iter=min(N_ITER, n_cand), scoring={'roc_auc': 'roc_auc', 'pr_auc': 'average_precision'},\n                            refit='roc_auc', cv=cv, random_state=SEED, n_jobs=-1)\n    fit_kw = {'sample_weight': compute_sample_weight('balanced', y_tr)} if fam == 'GRADIENTBOOSTING' else {}\n    rs.fit(X_tr, y_tr, **fit_kw)\n    i = rs.best_index_; cvr = rs.cv_results_\n    cv_tables[fam] = pd.DataFrame(cvr)[['params', 'mean_test_roc_auc', 'std_test_roc_auc', 'mean_test_pr_auc']].sort_values('mean_test_roc_auc', ascending=False)\n    m = rs.best_estimator_; p = {k: (v if isinstance(v, (int, float, str, type(None))) else str(v)) for k, v in rs.best_params_.items()}\n\n    # Held-out test set: reporting only, not used for selection\n    proba = m.predict_proba(X_te)[:, 1]; pred = (proba >= 0.5).astype(int)\n    tn, fp, fn, tp = confusion_matrix(y_te, pred, labels=[0, 1]).ravel()\n    met = dict(cv_roc_auc_mean=float(cvr['mean_test_roc_auc'][i]), cv_roc_auc_std=float(cvr['std_test_roc_auc'][i]),\n               cv_pr_auc=float(cvr['mean_test_pr_auc'][i]),\n               accuracy=accuracy_score(y_te, pred), precision=precision_score(y_te, pred, zero_division=0),\n               recall=recall_score(y_te, pred), f1=f1_score(y_te, pred), roc_auc=roc_auc_score(y_te, proba),\n               pr_auc=average_precision_score(y_te, proba), tn=float(tn), fp=float(fp), fn=float(fn), tp=float(tp))\n    run = f'{fam}_CV_{stamp}'\n    with exp.start_run(run):\n        exp.log_params({**p, 'family': fam, 'seed': SEED, 'test_size': 0.2, 'cv_folds': 5, 'n_iter': min(N_ITER, n_cand),\n                        'excluded_features': ','.join(LEAKAGE_COLS)})\n        exp.log_metrics(met)\n    results.append({'run': run, 'family': fam, 'params': p, **met}); models[run] = m\n    print(f'{fam:<17} CV ROC-AUC {met[\"cv_roc_auc_mean\"]:.3f} +/- {met[\"cv_roc_auc_std\"]:.3f} | test ROC-AUC {met[\"roc_auc\"]:.3f} | test PR-AUC {met[\"pr_auc\"]:.3f}')\n\n# Champion selected on CV only\nleaderboard = pd.DataFrame(results).sort_values('cv_roc_auc_mean', ascending=False).reset_index(drop=True)\nbest = leaderboard.iloc[0]; best_model = models[best['run']]\ngap = leaderboard.cv_roc_auc_mean.iloc[0] - leaderboard.cv_roc_auc_mean.iloc[1]\nprint('\\n' + leaderboard[['run', 'cv_roc_auc_mean', 'cv_roc_auc_std', 'cv_pr_auc', 'roc_auc', 'pr_auc', 'recall', 'precision', 'f1', 'tn', 'fp', 'fn', 'tp']].round(3).to_string(index=False))\nprint(f'\\nCHAMPION: {best[\"run\"]} {best[\"params\"]}')\nprint(f'Lead over #2 in CV ROC-AUC: {gap:.3f} (champion CV std {best[\"cv_roc_auc_std\"]:.3f})'\n      + (' -> statistically tied' if gap < best['cv_roc_auc_std'] else ''))\nprint('features used:', len(FEATURE_COLS), '| excluded:', LEAKAGE_COLS)",
      "outputs": [],
      "execution_count": null
    },
    {
      "id": "ad37bcd7-9e4a-4a31-a5b1-632f1cb503cd",
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "metadata": {
        "codeCollapsed": true,
        "collapsed": false
      },
      "source": "### Phase 3 Deliverables\n| Deliverable | Where |\n|---|---|\n| Best-performing model | `best_model` / `champion_summary` (selected by mean 5-fold CV ROC-AUC) |\n| Hyperparameter tuning summary | `tuning_summary` (per family, 20-candidate randomized CV search) + `cv_tables[family]` (all candidates) + `leaderboard`; also in experiment `CODE_BLUE_EXPERIMENT` |\n| Model evaluation report | ROC / PR curves, confusion matrix, classification report on the held-out test set (cell below) |\n| Feature importance analysis | `feature_importance_df` + chart |\n\n> Leakage features `LOS_DAYS` and `ADMISSION_DURATION_HRS` are excluded from training. Test metrics are from a held-out set not used for selection; with only 19 test positives, differences of ~0.02 ROC-AUC between families are within noise."
    },
    {
      "id": "bf5d833e-deed-4235-b165-0a86e924a4c9",
      "cell_type": "code",
      "metadata": {
        "language": "python",
        "title": "Phase 3 deliverable: champion and tuning summary"
      },
      "source": "champion_summary = pd.Series({'run': best['run'], 'algorithm': best['family'], 'params': best['params'],\n    **{k: round(float(best[k]), 4) for k in ['cv_roc_auc_mean', 'cv_roc_auc_std', 'cv_pr_auc', 'accuracy', 'precision', 'recall', 'f1', 'roc_auc', 'pr_auc']}})\ntuning_summary = pd.DataFrame([{\n    'family': fam, 'candidates': len(t),\n    'best_cv_roc_auc': t.mean_test_roc_auc.iloc[0], 'cv_std': t.std_test_roc_auc.iloc[0],\n    'worst_cv_roc_auc': t.mean_test_roc_auc.iloc[-1], 'best_cv_pr_auc': t.mean_test_pr_auc.max(),\n    'test_roc_auc': float(leaderboard.loc[leaderboard.family == fam, 'roc_auc'].iloc[0]),\n    'test_recall': float(leaderboard.loc[leaderboard.family == fam, 'recall'].iloc[0]),\n    'best_params': str(t.params.iloc[0])} for fam, t in cv_tables.items()]\n).sort_values('best_cv_roc_auc', ascending=False).round(4).reset_index(drop=True)\nprint(champion_summary.to_string())\ntuning_summary",
      "outputs": [],
      "execution_count": null
    },
    {
      "id": "5c0f0de7-4148-4b44-99a4-a92f1c755c25",
      "cell_type": "code",
      "metadata": {
        "language": "python",
        "title": "Phase 3 deliverable: model evaluation report"
      },
      "source": "import matplotlib.pyplot as plt\nfrom sklearn.metrics import roc_curve, precision_recall_curve, average_precision_score, classification_report, ConfusionMatrixDisplay\n\nte_proba = best_model.predict_proba(X_te)[:, 1]\nte_pred = (te_proba >= 0.5).astype(int)\nfpr, tpr, _ = roc_curve(y_te, te_proba)\nprec, rec, _ = precision_recall_curve(y_te, te_proba)\n\nfig, ax = plt.subplots(1, 3, figsize=(16, 4.5))\nax[0].plot(fpr, tpr, label=f'AUC = {roc_auc_score(y_te, te_proba):.3f}'); ax[0].plot([0, 1], [0, 1], 'k--', lw=0.8)\nax[0].set(title='ROC curve', xlabel='False positive rate', ylabel='True positive rate'); ax[0].legend()\nax[1].plot(rec, prec, label=f'AP = {average_precision_score(y_te, te_proba):.3f}'); ax[1].axhline(y_te.mean(), color='k', ls='--', lw=0.8)\nax[1].set(title='Precision-recall curve', xlabel='Recall', ylabel='Precision'); ax[1].legend()\nConfusionMatrixDisplay.from_predictions(y_te, te_pred, display_labels=['No Code Blue', 'Code Blue'], ax=ax[2], colorbar=False)\nax[2].set_title('Confusion matrix (threshold 0.5)')\nfig.suptitle(f'Champion: {best[\"run\"]}'); plt.tight_layout(); plt.show()\nprint(classification_report(y_te, te_pred, target_names=['No Code Blue', 'Code Blue'], digits=3))",
      "outputs": [],
      "execution_count": null
    },
    {
      "id": "93c40ef4-83c8-4e8c-95e1-0223a9e99ce2",
      "cell_type": "code",
      "metadata": {
        "language": "python",
        "title": "Phase 3 deliverable: feature importance analysis"
      },
      "source": "_est = best_model.named_steps['clf'] if hasattr(best_model, 'named_steps') else best_model\n_imp = _est.feature_importances_ if hasattr(_est, 'feature_importances_') else np.abs(_est.coef_[0])\nfeature_importance_df = (pd.DataFrame({'FEATURE': FEATURE_COLS, 'IMPORTANCE': _imp / _imp.sum()})\n    .sort_values('IMPORTANCE', ascending=False).reset_index(drop=True))\nfeature_importance_df['CUMULATIVE'] = feature_importance_df['IMPORTANCE'].cumsum()\ntop = feature_importance_df.head(15).iloc[::-1]\nplt.figure(figsize=(8, 6)); plt.barh(top.FEATURE, top.IMPORTANCE)\nplt.title(f'Top 15 feature importances ({best[\"family\"]})'); plt.xlabel('Normalized importance'); plt.tight_layout(); plt.show()\nfeature_importance_df.round(4)",
      "outputs": [],
      "execution_count": null
    },
    {
      "id": "4b2d7240-5d80-4020-93d7-f402d98f6215",
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "metadata": {
        "codeCollapsed": false
      },
      "source": "## Phase 4 - Model Registry deployment\nRegisters the champion as CODEBLUE_MODEL version V1_0 (warehouse target) with explainability enabled (SHAP explain function). Stored in version metadata: training metadata, performance metrics, model parameters, feature definitions and feature importance. V1_0 is set as the default (approved) version."
    },
    {
      "id": "31493201-89fd-4dfc-856b-2ffd0ae14f24",
      "cell_type": "code",
      "metadata": {
        "language": "python",
        "title": "Phase 4: register CODEBLUE_MODEL V1_0"
      },
      "source": "from snowflake.ml.registry import Registry\nreg = Registry(session=session, database_name=DB, schema_name=SCHEMA)\ntry:\n    reg.delete_model(MODEL_NAME)   # idempotent re-run inside DEMO_DB\nexcept Exception:\n    pass\n\nest = best_model.named_steps['clf'] if hasattr(best_model, 'named_steps') else best_model\nimp = est.feature_importances_ if hasattr(est, 'feature_importances_') else np.abs(est.coef_[0])\nfeature_importance = dict(sorted({f: float(v) for f, v in zip(FEATURE_COLS, imp / imp.sum())}.items(), key=lambda kv: -kv[1]))\nfeature_definitions = {'source_feature_view': f'{DB}.{FEATURES}.{FV_NAME}${FV_VERSION}', 'features': FEATURE_COLS,\n    'imputation': 'median', 'medians': {k: float(v) for k, v in medians.items()}, 'gender_label_encoding': gender_map}\nmetrics = {**{k: float(best[k]) for k in ['accuracy', 'precision', 'recall', 'f1', 'roc_auc']},\n    'confusion_matrix': {'tn': int(best.tn), 'fp': int(best.fp), 'fn': int(best.fn), 'tp': int(best.tp)},\n    'model_params': {k: (v if isinstance(v, (int, float, str, type(None))) else str(v)) for k, v in best['params'].items()},\n    'algorithm': best['family'], 'experiment': EXPERIMENT, 'run': best['run'],\n    'training_metadata': {'train_rows': int(len(X_tr)), 'test_rows': int(len(X_te)), 'positive_rate': float(y.mean()), 'seed': SEED, 'trained_at': str(pd.Timestamp.now())},\n    'feature_definitions': feature_definitions, 'feature_importance': feature_importance}\n\nlog_kwargs = dict(model_name=MODEL_NAME, version_name=MODEL_VERSION, sample_input_data=X_tr.head(100),\n    target_platforms=['WAREHOUSE'], metrics=metrics, comment=f'Code Blue risk model ({best[\"family\"]}) trained on {FV_NAME}/{FV_VERSION}')\ntry:\n    mv = reg.log_model(best_model, options={'enable_explainability': True}, **log_kwargs)\n    EXPLAIN_ENABLED = True\nexcept Exception as e:\n    print('explainability unavailable, registering without it:', str(e)[:200])\n    mv = reg.log_model(best_model, options={'enable_explainability': False}, **log_kwargs)\n    EXPLAIN_ENABLED = False\nreg.get_model(MODEL_NAME).default = MODEL_VERSION\nprint('Registered', FQ_MODEL, mv.version_name, '| explain:', EXPLAIN_ENABLED)\nprint([f['name'] for f in mv.show_functions()])\nprint('Top features:', list(feature_importance.items())[:8])",
      "outputs": [],
      "execution_count": null
    },
    {
      "id": "efc1f094-ceef-4853-8db9-1fb4169d4302",
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "metadata": {
        "codeCollapsed": true,
        "collapsed": false
      },
      "source": "### Phase 4 Deliverables\n| Deliverable | Where |\n|---|---|\n| Registered production-ready model | `DEMO_DB.CLINIC.CODEBLUE_MODEL` version `V1_0` (default version) |\n| Model Registry entry | `model_versions` (SHOW VERSIONS) |\n| Model metadata documentation | `model_metadata_doc` (cell below) |"
    },
    {
      "id": "e862c8ef-df1d-4d4b-92f8-bdc4784742a1",
      "cell_type": "code",
      "metadata": {
        "language": "sql",
        "resultVariableName": "model_versions",
        "title": "Phase 4 deliverable: Model Registry entry"
      },
      "source": "%%sql -r model_versions\nSHOW VERSIONS IN MODEL DEMO_DB.CLINIC.CODEBLUE_MODEL;",
      "outputs": [],
      "execution_count": null
    },
    {
      "id": "a5fcb800-4c21-4066-a8f0-a77c4179924d",
      "cell_type": "code",
      "metadata": {
        "language": "python",
        "title": "Phase 4 deliverable: model metadata documentation"
      },
      "source": "reg_metrics = mv.show_metrics()\nmodel_metadata_doc = pd.DataFrame([\n    ('Model', FQ_MODEL), ('Version', mv.version_name),\n    ('Default version', reg.get_model(MODEL_NAME).default.version_name),\n    ('Algorithm', reg_metrics.get('algorithm')), ('Experiment run', f\"{reg_metrics.get('experiment')} / {reg_metrics.get('run')}\"),\n    ('Comment', mv.comment), ('Target platform', 'WAREHOUSE'), ('Explainability enabled', EXPLAIN_ENABLED),\n    ('Functions', ', '.join(f['name'] for f in mv.show_functions())),\n    ('Source feature view', feature_definitions['source_feature_view']), ('Feature count', len(FEATURE_COLS)),\n    ('Training rows / test rows', f\"{reg_metrics['training_metadata']['train_rows']} / {reg_metrics['training_metadata']['test_rows']}\"),\n    ('Positive rate', round(reg_metrics['training_metadata']['positive_rate'], 4)),\n    ('Trained at', reg_metrics['training_metadata']['trained_at']),\n    ('Hyperparameters', reg_metrics.get('model_params')),\n    *[(f'Test {k}', round(reg_metrics[k], 4)) for k in ['accuracy', 'precision', 'recall', 'f1', 'roc_auc']],\n    ('Confusion matrix', reg_metrics.get('confusion_matrix')),\n], columns=['PROPERTY', 'VALUE'])\nmodel_metadata_doc['VALUE'] = model_metadata_doc['VALUE'].astype(str)\nmodel_metadata_doc",
      "outputs": [],
      "execution_count": null
    },
    {
      "id": "17c6697a-63b2-4c87-ac37-7e1ff827ff5b",
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "metadata": {
        "codeCollapsed": false
      },
      "source": "## Phase 5 - Production inference\nLoads the default (approved) CODEBLUE_MODEL version, retrieves features for all 1,000 encounters from the same feature view (identical pipeline), and scores with predict_proba (threshold 0.5) plus per-row SHAP explanations (top 5 drivers with direction). Results go to CODEBLUE_SCORING_RESULTS."
    },
    {
      "id": "2aa63362-0853-4ad9-a589-639b7ab82a42",
      "cell_type": "code",
      "metadata": {
        "language": "python",
        "title": "Phase 5: batch scoring + explanations"
      },
      "source": "prod_mv = Registry(session=session, database_name=DB, schema_name=SCHEMA).get_model(MODEL_NAME).default\nscore_spine = session.table(f'{DB}.{SCHEMA}.PATIENT_CODEBLUE').select('PRIMARYMRN', F.col('ENTRY_DATE').alias('ENCOUNTER_TS'))\ninf_pdf = fs.retrieve_feature_values(spine_df=score_spine, features=[fv], spine_timestamp_col='ENCOUNTER_TS').to_pandas().reset_index(drop=True)\nXs = inf_pdf[FEATURE_COLS].astype('float64')\n\nproba_out = prod_mv.run(Xs, function_name='predict_proba')\nout_cols = [c for c in proba_out.columns if c not in FEATURE_COLS]\np1 = proba_out[out_cols[-1]].astype(float).values\n\ntry:\n    ex = prod_mv.run(Xs, function_name='explain')\n    ex_cols = [c for c in ex.columns if c not in FEATURE_COLS]\n    shap = ex[ex_cols].astype(float).values\n    ex_feats = [c.replace('_explanation', '').replace('_EXPLANATION', '') for c in ex_cols]\n    method = 'SHAP'\nexcept Exception as e:\n    print('explain failed, using importance x z-score fallback:', str(e)[:150])\n    z = ((Xs - X_tr.mean()) / X_tr.std().replace(0, 1)).values\n    shap = z * np.array([feature_importance[f] for f in FEATURE_COLS]); ex_feats = FEATURE_COLS; method = 'IMPORTANCE_X_ZSCORE'\n\ndef rationale(i):\n    order = np.argsort(-np.abs(shap[i]))[:5]\n    drivers = [{'feature': ex_feats[j], 'value': round(float(Xs.iloc[i][ex_feats[j]]), 3) if ex_feats[j] in Xs else None,\n                'contribution': round(float(shap[i][j]), 4), 'direction': 'increases risk' if shap[i][j] > 0 else 'decreases risk'} for j in order]\n    return json.dumps({'method': method, 'top_drivers': drivers})\n\nscoring = pd.DataFrame({'PRIMARYMRN': inf_pdf['PRIMARYMRN'], 'CODEBLUE_PREDICTION': (p1 >= 0.5).astype(int),\n    'CODEBLUE_PROBABILITY': p1.round(4), 'MODEL_VERSION': f'{MODEL_NAME}/{prod_mv.version_name}',\n    'SCORING_TIMESTAMP': pd.Timestamp.now(), 'EXPLAINABILITY_JSON': [rationale(i) for i in range(len(Xs))]})\nsession.write_pandas(scoring, 'TMP_CODEBLUE_SCORES', database=DB, schema=SCHEMA, auto_create_table=True, overwrite=True, use_logical_type=True)\nsession.sql(f'''CREATE OR REPLACE TABLE {DB}.{SCHEMA}.CODEBLUE_SCORING_RESULTS AS\nSELECT PRIMARYMRN, CODEBLUE_PREDICTION, CODEBLUE_PROBABILITY, MODEL_VERSION, SCORING_TIMESTAMP::TIMESTAMP_NTZ AS SCORING_TIMESTAMP,\n       PARSE_JSON(EXPLAINABILITY_JSON) AS EXPLAINABILITY_ATTRIBUTES FROM {DB}.{SCHEMA}.TMP_CODEBLUE_SCORES''').collect()\nsession.sql(f'DROP TABLE IF EXISTS {DB}.{SCHEMA}.TMP_CODEBLUE_SCORES').collect()\nprint('scored rows:', session.table(f'{DB}.{SCHEMA}.CODEBLUE_SCORING_RESULTS').count(), '| predicted positives:', int(scoring.CODEBLUE_PREDICTION.sum()))",
      "outputs": [],
      "execution_count": null
    },
    {
      "id": "f3db6f72-c6b5-4dc3-bd7c-940333cf1311",
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "metadata": {
        "codeCollapsed": true,
        "collapsed": false
      },
      "source": "### Phase 5 Deliverables\n| Deliverable | Where |\n|---|---|\n| CODEBLUE_SCORING_RESULTS table | `DEMO_DB.CLINIC.CODEBLUE_SCORING_RESULTS` (created above) |\n| Prediction summary report | `prediction_summary` |\n| Risk distribution analysis | `risk_distribution` (bands: Low < 0.3, Medium 0.3-0.7, High >= 0.7) + histogram |"
    },
    {
      "id": "463b21b9-82e9-4aea-a2a2-e5213efd959f",
      "cell_type": "code",
      "metadata": {
        "language": "sql",
        "resultVariableName": "prediction_summary",
        "title": "Phase 5 deliverable: prediction summary report"
      },
      "source": "%%sql -r prediction_summary\nSELECT ANY_VALUE(MODEL_VERSION) AS MODEL_VERSION, MAX(SCORING_TIMESTAMP) AS SCORED_AT,\n       COUNT(*) AS SCORED_PATIENTS, SUM(CODEBLUE_PREDICTION) AS PREDICTED_CODEBLUE,\n       ROUND(AVG(CODEBLUE_PREDICTION) * 100, 2) AS PREDICTED_POSITIVE_PCT,\n       ROUND(AVG(CODEBLUE_PROBABILITY), 4) AS AVG_PROBABILITY, ROUND(MEDIAN(CODEBLUE_PROBABILITY), 4) AS MEDIAN_PROBABILITY,\n       ROUND(MAX(CODEBLUE_PROBABILITY), 4) AS MAX_PROBABILITY\nFROM DEMO_DB.CLINIC.CODEBLUE_SCORING_RESULTS;",
      "outputs": [],
      "execution_count": null
    },
    {
      "id": "ed7b41df-cfe4-4ce2-b10e-cb6db2bd4f26",
      "cell_type": "code",
      "metadata": {
        "language": "sql",
        "resultVariableName": "risk_distribution",
        "title": "Phase 5 deliverable: risk distribution by band"
      },
      "source": "%%sql -r risk_distribution\nSELECT CASE WHEN CODEBLUE_PROBABILITY >= 0.7 THEN '3-High' WHEN CODEBLUE_PROBABILITY >= 0.3 THEN '2-Medium' ELSE '1-Low' END AS RISK_BAND,\n       COUNT(*) AS PATIENTS, ROUND(COUNT(*) * 100 / SUM(COUNT(*)) OVER (), 1) AS PCT_OF_PATIENTS,\n       ROUND(AVG(CODEBLUE_PROBABILITY), 4) AS AVG_PROBABILITY, SUM(CODEBLUE_PREDICTION) AS PREDICTED_CODEBLUE\nFROM DEMO_DB.CLINIC.CODEBLUE_SCORING_RESULTS\nGROUP BY 1 ORDER BY 1;",
      "outputs": [],
      "execution_count": null
    },
    {
      "id": "34ca6238-5d99-48bb-a8e9-ba851594aa81",
      "cell_type": "code",
      "metadata": {
        "language": "python",
        "title": "Phase 5 deliverable: probability histogram"
      },
      "source": "import matplotlib.pyplot as plt\nplt.figure(figsize=(9, 4))\nplt.hist(p1, bins=40, color='steelblue', edgecolor='white')\nfor t, lbl in [(0.3, 'Medium'), (0.7, 'High')]:\n    plt.axvline(t, color='red', ls='--', lw=1); plt.text(t + 0.01, plt.ylim()[1] * 0.9, lbl, color='red')\nplt.yscale('log'); plt.title('Code Blue probability distribution (log count)')\nplt.xlabel('Predicted probability'); plt.ylabel('Patients'); plt.tight_layout(); plt.show()",
      "outputs": [],
      "execution_count": null
    },
    {
      "id": "30b90032-bb3a-4841-a50c-6c8ed8d6702c",
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "metadata": {
        "codeCollapsed": false
      },
      "source": "## Phase 6 - Final business-ready dataset\nLEFT JOIN of PATIENT_CODEBLUE with CODEBLUE_SCORING_RESULTS on PRIMARYMRN (one row per encounter), retaining all source fields and appending prediction, probability, model version, scoring timestamp and explainability attributes."
    },
    {
      "id": "6ccf78bd-f4dc-4267-8119-a6e80d7ead33",
      "cell_type": "code",
      "metadata": {
        "language": "sql",
        "resultVariableName": "final_create",
        "title": "Phase 6: create CODEBLUE_PREDICTION_RESULTS"
      },
      "source": "%%sql -r final_create\nCREATE OR REPLACE TABLE DEMO_DB.CLINIC.CODEBLUE_PREDICTION_RESULTS AS\nSELECT p.*, s.CODEBLUE_PREDICTION, s.CODEBLUE_PROBABILITY, s.MODEL_VERSION, s.SCORING_TIMESTAMP, s.EXPLAINABILITY_ATTRIBUTES\nFROM DEMO_DB.CLINIC.PATIENT_CODEBLUE p\nLEFT JOIN DEMO_DB.CLINIC.CODEBLUE_SCORING_RESULTS s ON p.PRIMARYMRN = s.PRIMARYMRN;",
      "outputs": [],
      "execution_count": null
    },
    {
      "id": "9caf20b4-4b35-47b5-adfa-5f1e2e150419",
      "cell_type": "code",
      "metadata": {
        "language": "sql",
        "resultVariableName": "final_summary",
        "title": "Phase 6: validate final dataset"
      },
      "source": "%%sql -r final_summary\nSELECT COUNT(*) AS TOTAL_RECORDS, COUNT(CODEBLUE_PROBABILITY) AS SCORED, SUM(CODEBLUE) AS ACTUAL_CODEBLUE,\n       SUM(CODEBLUE_PREDICTION) AS PREDICTED_CODEBLUE, SUM(IFF(CODEBLUE=1 AND CODEBLUE_PREDICTION=1,1,0)) AS TRUE_POSITIVES,\n       ROUND(AVG(DATEDIFF('hour', ENTRY_DATE, DISCHARGE_DATE))/24,1) AS AVG_LOS_DAYS,\n       ROUND(AVG(IFF(CODEBLUE=1, DATEDIFF('hour', ENTRY_DATE, DISCHARGE_DATE)/24, NULL)),1) AS AVG_LOS_CODEBLUE,\n       COUNT_IF(CODEBLUE_PROBABILITY >= 0.7) AS HIGH_RISK_PATIENTS, ANY_VALUE(MODEL_VERSION) AS MODEL_VERSION\nFROM DEMO_DB.CLINIC.CODEBLUE_PREDICTION_RESULTS;",
      "outputs": [],
      "execution_count": null
    },
    {
      "id": "e7c8e8c4-a6ed-4e7a-b87f-d4ac16aeed90",
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "metadata": {
        "codeCollapsed": false
      },
      "source": "### Phase 6 Deliverables\n| Deliverable | Where |\n|---|---|\n| Fully enriched patient prediction dataset | `DEMO_DB.CLINIC.CODEBLUE_PREDICTION_RESULTS` (all source columns + predictions) |\n| Prediction probability scores | `CODEBLUE_PROBABILITY` / `CODEBLUE_PREDICTION` columns (`enriched_sample`) |\n| Explainability insights | `explainability_insights` (top risk drivers among high-risk patients) |\n| Business-ready analytical dataset | view `DEMO_DB.CLINIC.CODEBLUE_PATIENT_RISK_V` (`business_ready_sample`) |"
    },
    {
      "id": "9816e733-3565-4046-87b8-ac7c29d1d762",
      "cell_type": "code",
      "metadata": {
        "language": "sql",
        "resultVariableName": "enriched_sample",
        "title": "Phase 6 deliverable: enriched dataset with probability scores"
      },
      "source": "%%sql -r enriched_sample\nSELECT PRIMARYMRN, AGE, GENDER, CODEBLUE, CODEBLUE_PREDICTION, CODEBLUE_PROBABILITY, MODEL_VERSION, SCORING_TIMESTAMP\nFROM DEMO_DB.CLINIC.CODEBLUE_PREDICTION_RESULTS\nORDER BY CODEBLUE_PROBABILITY DESC\nLIMIT 20;",
      "outputs": [],
      "execution_count": null
    },
    {
      "id": "ed4a3470-c66d-4446-bfe1-18e9cf397326",
      "cell_type": "code",
      "metadata": {
        "language": "sql",
        "resultVariableName": "explainability_insights",
        "title": "Phase 6 deliverable: explainability insights (high-risk drivers)"
      },
      "source": "%%sql -r explainability_insights\nSELECT d.value:feature::STRING AS RISK_DRIVER,\n       COUNT_IF(d.index = 0) AS TIMES_TOP_DRIVER,\n       COUNT(*) AS TIMES_IN_TOP5,\n       ROUND(COUNT(*) * 100 / ANY_VALUE(t.HIGH_RISK), 1) AS PCT_HIGH_RISK_PATIENTS,\n       ROUND(AVG(d.value:contribution::FLOAT), 4) AS AVG_CONTRIBUTION,\n       COUNT_IF(d.value:direction::STRING = 'increases risk') AS TIMES_INCREASES_RISK\nFROM DEMO_DB.CLINIC.CODEBLUE_PREDICTION_RESULTS r,\n     LATERAL FLATTEN(input => r.EXPLAINABILITY_ATTRIBUTES:top_drivers) d,\n     (SELECT COUNT_IF(CODEBLUE_PROBABILITY >= 0.7) AS HIGH_RISK FROM DEMO_DB.CLINIC.CODEBLUE_PREDICTION_RESULTS) t\nWHERE r.CODEBLUE_PROBABILITY >= 0.7\nGROUP BY 1\nORDER BY TIMES_TOP_DRIVER DESC, TIMES_IN_TOP5 DESC;",
      "outputs": [],
      "execution_count": null
    },
    {
      "id": "3ede1059-d9e7-4165-aee2-c330bd5068a8",
      "cell_type": "code",
      "metadata": {
        "language": "sql",
        "resultVariableName": "business_view_create",
        "title": "Phase 6 deliverable: business-ready view"
      },
      "source": "%%sql -r business_view_create\nCREATE OR REPLACE VIEW DEMO_DB.CLINIC.CODEBLUE_PATIENT_RISK_V\nCOMMENT = 'Business-ready Code Blue risk dataset: one row per patient encounter with risk band and top drivers'\nAS\nSELECT PRIMARYMRN, AGE, GENDER, ENTRY_DATE AS ADMISSION_TS, DISCHARGE_DATE AS DISCHARGE_TS,\n       ROUND(DATEDIFF('hour', ENTRY_DATE, DISCHARGE_DATE) / 24, 1) AS LENGTH_OF_STAY_DAYS,\n       RESPIRATION, SYSTOLIC_BP, PULSE, PULSE_OXIMETRY, TEMPERATURE, BNP, ALBUMIN, BLOOD_CULTURE,\n       CODEBLUE AS ACTUAL_CODEBLUE, CODEBLUE_PREDICTION AS PREDICTED_CODEBLUE,\n       ROUND(CODEBLUE_PROBABILITY * 100, 1) AS RISK_SCORE_PCT,\n       CASE WHEN CODEBLUE_PROBABILITY >= 0.7 THEN 'High' WHEN CODEBLUE_PROBABILITY > 0.3 THEN 'Medium' ELSE 'Low' END AS RISK_BAND,\n       EXPLAINABILITY_ATTRIBUTES:top_drivers[0]:feature::STRING AS TOP_RISK_DRIVER_1,\n       EXPLAINABILITY_ATTRIBUTES:top_drivers[1]:feature::STRING AS TOP_RISK_DRIVER_2,\n       EXPLAINABILITY_ATTRIBUTES:top_drivers[2]:feature::STRING AS TOP_RISK_DRIVER_3,\n       EXPLAINABILITY_ATTRIBUTES:method::STRING AS EXPLANATION_METHOD,\n       MODEL_VERSION, SCORING_TIMESTAMP\nFROM DEMO_DB.CLINIC.CODEBLUE_PREDICTION_RESULTS;",
      "outputs": [],
      "execution_count": null
    },
    {
      "id": "50657f2b-321c-4275-ab39-630cad7bfc25",
      "cell_type": "code",
      "metadata": {
        "language": "sql",
        "resultVariableName": "business_ready_sample",
        "title": "Phase 6 deliverable: business-ready dataset preview"
      },
      "source": "%%sql -r business_ready_sample\nSELECT RISK_BAND, COUNT(*) AS PATIENTS, ROUND(AVG(RISK_SCORE_PCT), 1) AS AVG_RISK_SCORE_PCT,\n       SUM(ACTUAL_CODEBLUE) AS ACTUAL_CODEBLUE, SUM(PREDICTED_CODEBLUE) AS PREDICTED_CODEBLUE,\n       MODE(TOP_RISK_DRIVER_1) AS MOST_COMMON_TOP_DRIVER\nFROM DEMO_DB.CLINIC.CODEBLUE_PATIENT_RISK_V\nGROUP BY 1 ORDER BY AVG_RISK_SCORE_PCT DESC;",
      "outputs": [],
      "execution_count": null
    }
  ]
}*
